{"type":"text","timestamp":1787412359079,"sessionID":"ses_fd5edbfeaffeSYZMb1IjX9fheY","part":{"id":"prt_02a1422000018clTdA4KxPI58h","messageID":"msg_02a14077c001o0ESdWlGztDMtR","sessionID":"ses_fd5edbfeaffeSYZMb1IjX9fheY","type":"text","text":"All behaviors work as specified. The change is complete and confined to `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- `ignore` (single glob or array) excludes matching inputs; evaluated via a sub-matcher built with callbacks stripped so it doesn't inherit the caller's `onResult`/`onMatch`/`onIgnore`.\n- `onResult` fires once per input; `onMatch` only when matching; `onIgnore` only when excluded by an ignore pattern.\n- Result object carries `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, `isMatch` (final decision).\n- Inputs that never matched the pattern are reported as non-match, never ignored.\n- Existing behavior (array patterns, `returnObject`, `returnState`) is unchanged, and the pre-existing test failures are unaffected by my edit (same 3 pass / 5 fail on the original code).","time":{"start":1787412357633,"end":1787412359072}}}
